  "description": "Ultra high-performance CSV, Fixed-Width, Excel (.xlsx), and JSONL file parser and writer for .NET 8+. SIMD-accelerated parsing (AVX-512/AVX2/NEON) with a zero-allocation, fixed-112-byte read hot path: UTF-8 reading is ~12% faster than Sep and CSV writing is 2-3x faster, both at a fraction of the memory. RFC 4180 compliant with fluent read/write APIs. Fixed-Width support includes field alignment, padding, overflow handling, and async streaming. Excel reading and writing with zero extra dependencies. JSONL targets AI/ML pipelines: OpenAI/Anthropic LLM fine-tuning shapes, CSV-to-JSONL conversion, embedding-API batching, an inline vector parser, and AOT-safe JsonTypeInfo. Includes async I/O, source generators for native AOT, IDataReader/DbDataReader bridges, PipeReader streaming, LINQ-style extensions, progress reporting, and custom type converters.",
  "id": "HeroParser",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-05-29T13:26:52.62Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "tbi8QhuQV2Q7UBL32AE9FmBc1Ws0Nlu2swvc3fo2d1OqbLttMensOdjxsg6HNkznTv2dsJbYA+3HJLUxHSrSVQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 1269741,
  "published": "2026-05-29T13:23:40.15Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.3.0 introduces five high-performance, Native AOT-compliant AI-native tabular capabilities: an LLM structured output repair binder (LlmRepair), a zero-allocation tabular vector embedding batching pipeline (ToLlmEmbeddingsAsync), an AI-driven tabular context profiler (TabularContextProfiler) rendering statistical markdown cards, a reflection-free agent tool argument mapper (SchemaMetadata.MapFromToolCall) enforcing all [Validate] constraints, and a token-bounded JSON array chunker (JsonLlmChunker) utilizing AOT-safe JsonTypeInfo. Full changelog: https://github.com/KoalaFacts/HeroParser/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
